        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear Colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital course of your 70-year-old female patient, admitted on 24/10/2014 with an acute exacerbation of her known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, she presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Diagnostic workup included chest X-ray confirming hyperinflation, arterial blood gas analysis revealing hypoxaemia, and blood tests showing mild inflammatory response. Pulse oximetry was monitored continuously. She was treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, supplemental oxygen therapy, and supportive intravenous fluids. She responded well to treatment with significant clinical improvement. At discharge, she was stable with satisfactory oxygen saturation on room air. We recommend continuation of her inhaled therapy and close outpatient follow-up. Pulmonary rehabilitation referral has been advised. Please do not hesitate to contact us should you require further information.</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "8648-8",
